      "handle": "@lelap_sparta",
      "isoDate": "1977-01-18T19:15:00",
      "displayDate": "Jan 18, 1977 • 7:15 PM",
      "content": "If the price of hogs has dropped 50% for the farmers, why am I still paying full price for pork chops at the grocery store? Somebody is making a lot of money in the middle while we all struggle.",
      "person_id": "p_010",
      "sourcePdf": "temp/North%20Kent%20Leader%20-%2001-19-1977%20-%20Page%206.pdf"
    },
    {
      "id": "post_pork_03",
      "type": "post",
      "author": "Jim White",
      "handle": "@jwhite_industry",
      "isoDate": "1977-01-18T20:00:00",
      "displayDate": "Jan 18, 1977 • 8:00 PM",
      "content": "It's important to remember that the 'farm dollar' only accounts for about 40 cents of the retail food price. The other 60 cents goes into processing, packaging, and shipping after the product leaves the farm gate.",
      "person_id": "p_101",
      "sourcePdf": "temp/North%20Kent%20Leader%20-%2001-19-1977%20-%20Page%206.pdf"
    },
    {
      "id": "post_pork_04",
